From a0995f4c5b3877dd8f6d4cc0dec83811cd422160 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soyjxck <soyjxck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 21:55:05 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 03/13] Cached getenv on hot paths; XInput probes empty slots
 once a second

The runtime's diagnostics are switched by environment variables read where
they are used, some of them per FIFO drain, per SPURS job or per event-queue
receive. On Windows getenv takes the CRT's lock and scans the environment
block: it showed up as strchr, 7% of Drakengard 3's render thread and 11% of
the RSX walker. ps3emu/env_cache.h answers from a table keyed on the address
of the name (a string literal), filled once; a file opts in by defining
getenv to ps3_env after its includes. Twelve files do. The replay harness
and the D3D12 engine's frame dump, which read a variable that changes at run
time, do not.

cellPad: XInputGetState on a slot with nothing plugged in enumerates devices
(DeviceIoControl, DevObjEnumDeviceInfo). The sweep of empty slots every 4 ms
was 4-11% of the wait samples of the game's main thread. Empty slots are now
probed once a second, and slots past XUSER_MAX_COUNT never.

Neither moved the frame rate measurably on its own (49-52 fps in the battle
benchmark either way); they take the two items off the profile.

Ported to SARPBC-recomp (T008) from soyjxck/ps3recomp 0e967d8dc827 (MIT),
libs/input part only; the original author is kept.
---
 libs/input/cellPad.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/input/cellPad.c b/libs/input/cellPad.c
index 1b12017..fac6d42 100644
--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -239,13 +239,24 @@ static void pad_poll_keyboard(void)
 
 static void pad_poll_xinput(void)
 {
+    /* An empty slot is re-probed once a second, not on every sweep. Asking
+     * XInput about a slot with nothing plugged in makes it enumerate devices
+     * (DeviceIoControl, DevObjEnumDeviceInfo): the sweep of empty slots every
+     * 4 ms was 4-11% of the wait samples of Drakengard 3's main thread, the
+     * thread that polls the pad. A controller plugged in mid-game appears
+     * within a second; XInput has four user slots, so the rest never exist. */
+    static ULONGLONG next_probe[PAD_MAX_HOST_PORTS];
+    const ULONGLONG now = GetTickCount64();
     for (int i = 0; i < PAD_MAX_HOST_PORTS; i++) {
         XINPUT_STATE state;
         memset(&state, 0, sizeof(state));
+        if (i >= XUSER_MAX_COUNT) { s_host_state[i].connected = 0; continue; }
+        if (!s_host_state[i].connected && now < next_probe[i]) continue;
 
         DWORD result = XInputGetState((DWORD)i, &state);
         if (result != ERROR_SUCCESS) {
             s_host_state[i].connected = 0;
+            next_probe[i] = now + 1000;
             continue;
         }
 
-- 
