From d4817b7c4c56b991c99d96246f33548191890c1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soyjxck <soyjxck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 10:03:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] d3d12: build triangle pipeline states on the build
 thread, not at first draw

The draw engine builds a pipeline (HLSL compile) on its own thread
(RSX_ASYNC_SHADERS), but the D3D12 pipeline state object -- the driver's
compile -- was still made at the pipeline's first draw, on the walker, at
encode time. With the driver's shader cache warm that is ~0.4 ms apiece
(235 in a 2-minute run, ~92 ms, all on the walker); for a shader the driver
has not seen, as in a new area, it is tens of milliseconds, and the frame
waits. The triangle-class state is now built right after the pipeline, on
the build thread (points and lines, rare, still on first use; RSX_PSO_PREWARM=0
restores first-use for all). Same run: 244 built, none on the walker.

Also:
- RSX_PSO_LOG=1: each pipeline state built, its time and its thread.
- RSX_HITCH_LOG lines carry the walker's work in the frame: textures
  uploaded, vertex conversions, pipelines and pipeline states built, draws.
- cellPad: PAD_STICK_FILE may hold "lx ly rx ry", so a script can steer and
  turn the camera (dod3-recomp's autoplay combat mode).

Replay regression: 102 frames identical to out/rep_win (rsx_replay rebuilt).

