From aa8dc53cb23b6437efa86c7e75bcef6910379574 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soyjxck <soyjxck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 03:05:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 07/13] cellPad SDL2: the pad on a thread of its own, rumble
 held until changed

SDL_GameControllerUpdate also runs every driver's device detection, and
on Windows a pad plugged in or out makes that enumerate the DirectInput
and HID devices on the calling thread, with the joystick lock held:
hundreds of milliseconds to seconds. Polled from the game thread, one
plug event stalled Drakengard 3 for 3 s (4 fps over the next five
seconds). So the guest never calls SDL now: a pad thread starts the
subsystem, polls every PAD_POLL_INTERVAL_MS, keeps the latest state of
every port, and applies the rumble the guest asked for; the guest's poll
copies that snapshot and its actuator call leaves a request, both under
a mutex the pad thread holds only for the copy. On Windows the thread
also dispatches its own message queue, which is where SDL's HID
discovery window delivers device changes.

Rumble: SDL's has a duration and the guest's actuator call does not (a
DS3 rumbles until told otherwise), so a non-zero request is re-sent
every 50 ms.

Tested on Windows through twelve hands-off runs of Drakengard 3 (the
thread up, input through PAD_FILE). A pad plugged in and out with the
thread in place is still to be tried with one to hand.

Ported to SARPBC-recomp (T008) from soyjxck/ps3recomp cd2ab9b04c12 (MIT),
libs/input part only; the original author is kept.
