From b4f1cc8d1242fc98b3e1eba695204c30b280e3f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soyjxck <soyjxck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 14:00:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 10/13] rsx metal: the window's mouse, modifier keys and mouse
 buttons, for a port played with them

rsx_host_mouse.h had only its Windows half; on macOS the calls did
nothing. The Metal backend owns the window there, so it implements them:

- rsx_host_mouse_capture: while asked for and the window is key, the
  cursor is put at the middle of the picture, hidden, and detached from
  the mouse (CGAssociateMouseAndMouseCursorPosition), so it cannot leave
  the window or reach the Dock; the mouse's events still carry its motion.
  Given back the moment the window is not key, and at shutdown.
- motion from the events' deltas (points; fractions carried over), the
  wheel as notches in the device's own direction whatever "natural
  scrolling" says (an event a notch for a wheel, 40 points a notch for a
  trackpad, its glide ignored).
- While the cursor is held the mouse's events stop at the event monitor,
  so a click cannot land on a title bar under the hidden cursor; otherwise
  they are AppKit's as before.
- rsx_metal_backend_mouse_button_down, and Shift, Control and Option in
  rsx_metal_backend_key_down: those keys send no key event, only a change
  of flags, whose per-side bits are now recorded under their keycodes.

rsx_host_mouse.c leaves the Apple build to the backend (its stubs stay for
every other system). cellPad hands a port's host-input function the Metal
window's focus, as it does the Win32 window's.

PS3RECOMP_METAL_EVENT_FILE=<path>: lines of key / flags / move / button /
wheel become events sent to the window through that same monitor, for a
run with no one at the keyboard. Checked with it in Drakengard 3: a key,
two keys at once, left Shift, both mouse buttons, the wheel both ways and
Escape each reach the pad as bound; 100 counts of motion arrive as 100;
the cursor is visible again after the process is killed while holding it.
The headless end-to-end step's 18 invocations pass. Not checked: a real
mouse or trackpad in the hand (the cursor's hiding, the feel of the
deltas).

Ported to SARPBC-recomp (T008) from soyjxck/ps3recomp c231b9df3d5d (MIT),
libs/input part only; the original author is kept.
