From 65a7f59607e5a710a19628e6d4d89e7d8de4bb76 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soyjxck <soyjxck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 16:35:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 11/13] "The first N times" gates stop counting at N

The gate that flooded (21f2763) was one of some three hundred of the same
shape in the runtime and the HLE libraries:

    static int n; if (n++ < 8) fprintf(stderr, ...);

The counter goes up on every call whether or not anything is printed, so
on a path called often enough it passes INT_MAX, turns negative, and the
gate is open again for the next 2^31 calls. How long that takes is only a
matter of the call rate: hours on the syscall, HLE-dispatch, SPU channel
and DMA paths, days on a per-draw one. Rather than judge each one's rate,
every one outside the five renderer files being worked on elsewhere
(rsx_draw_engine.c/.h, rsx_d3d12_engine.c, rsx_vulkan_engine.c,
rsx_vulkan_encode.inc) now stops counting once it has shut:

  304  x++ < N  ->  (x < N && ++x), and the like for <= and ++x: true on
       the same calls, the counter the same wherever the gate is open
    4  (x <= N && x++ < N): the counter is read again as `x <= N` after
       the gate, so it has to reach N + 1, and stops there
    6  made unsigned instead: the counter also paces a periodic line
       (x % 2000), so it must go on counting; it wraps to 0, not below it
    6  "print the first N, say 'suppressed' once, n++;": the increment on
       its own becomes `if (n <= N) n++;`

Unsigned and 64-bit counters were already safe and are untouched.

tools/audit_log_gates.py finds both shapes, rewrites with --fix the gates
that are nothing more than a gate, and reports the rest with every other
read of the counter for a person to decide (its docstring says how); it
exits 1 when anything is left, so it can serve as a check. On this tree
with those five files excluded it finds nothing; in them, 20.

One of the hand-decided ones I first got wrong: the file-read log's
counter (ppu_fs.cpp) also paces "[fs] read summary", which stopped
appearing. Comparing the log of a 250 s run with one from before the
change showed it; it is one of the six unsigned ones now, and the tool no
longer excuses a line as "only a print argument" when the counter is used
another way on it.

Checked: each rewritten form against the original call by call for
limits 0-40 (identical); the macOS workflow's standalone tests, the
headless end-to-end step's 18 invocations and the replay regression
(frame for frame as before); two 250 s runs of Drakengard 3's chapter 1
battle, whose logs have the same number of lines of every kind as a run
from before the change in 226 of 234 kinds, the other eight being paced by
time or by the run's length. The Windows-only parts (rsx_d3d12_backend.c)
are not compiled here.

