From 5d4219ae1da1ad19992d704689988ebf7c93a124 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: soyjxck <soyjxck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 18:16:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] cellPad, cellAudio: SDL leaves SIGINT and SIGTERM alone

SDL's events subsystem, which the pad and the audio device each bring up,
installs handlers for SIGINT and SIGTERM that only queue an SDL_QUIT
event. Outside the Linux Vulkan backend nothing reads SDL's events -- the
window is the Metal or the Win32 one -- so the process ignored Ctrl-C in a
terminal and `kill` alike. A benchmark harness's kill at 180 s was
ignored that way and the game ran for 18 hours.

SDL_HINT_NO_SIGNAL_HANDLERS is set before either subsystem starts (either
may be first), except where PS3RECOMP_RSX_VULKAN is defined: that
backend's window is SDL's and its pump acts on the event.

Drakengard 3 on macOS, signalled 25 s after launch with the pad and the
audio device up: before, still running 10 s after SIGTERM; now gone
0.17 s after SIGTERM and 0.10 s after SIGINT, ended by the signal. The
cursor a port holds is back afterwards (the window server's doing).

Ported to SARPBC-recomp (T008) from soyjxck/ps3recomp f58d67dee687 (MIT),
libs/input part only; the original author is kept.
---
 libs/input/cellPad.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libs/input/cellPad.c b/libs/input/cellPad.c
index 1261cb9..1c6e96c 100644
--- a/libs/input/cellPad.c
+++ b/libs/input/cellPad.c
@@ -349,6 +349,16 @@ static int pad_sdl_start(void)
      * the DirectInput/XInput device-notification window and re-checks the
      * XInput slots by itself. */
     SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_JOYSTICK_THREAD, "1");
+#endif
+#if defined(SDL_HINT_NO_SIGNAL_HANDLERS) && !defined(PS3RECOMP_RSX_VULKAN)
+    /* SDL's events subsystem, which the pad brings up with it, takes SIGINT
+     * and SIGTERM for itself and turns each into an SDL_QUIT event. Nothing
+     * here reads SDL's events -- the window is not SDL's -- so the process
+     * then ignored Ctrl-C and `kill` alike, and only SIGKILL ended it. The
+     * signals are left as the system has them. (Not under the Linux Vulkan
+     * backend: its window is SDL's and its pump acts on that event.) The
+     * audio backend says the same, as either may start SDL first. */
+    SDL_SetHint(SDL_HINT_NO_SIGNAL_HANDLERS, "1");
 #endif
     if (SDL_WasInit(SDL_INIT_GAMECONTROLLER) == 0 &&
         SDL_InitSubSystem(SDL_INIT_GAMECONTROLLER) != 0) {
-- 
